          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %em allegory
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            with properties meant to reflect properties that hold in a category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rel"} Rel
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relations"} relations
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories%2C+Allegories"} Categories, Allegories
            (
            %a{:href => "#FreydScedrov"}> Freyd-Scedrov
            ).
          %p
            Freyd and Scedrov argue that a categorical calculus of relations is an alternative and often more amenable framework for developing concepts traditionally couched in “functional” language (i.e., concepts which apply to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
            and
            = succeed ");" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            %em raison d’etre
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+categories"} regular categories
            is precisely that one can do
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relational+calculus"} relational calculus
            in them (as had been long known, e.g.,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"} Saunders MacLane
            showed how to calculate with relations to do
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram+chasing"} diagram chases
            in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+categories"} abelian categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory+of+relations"} bicategories of relations
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+and+exact+completion"} regular and exact completions
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/realizability+topos"} realizability toposes
          %p
            A signal feature of allegories is emphasis on the
            %em modular law
            (see def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Allegory"}
            below), which generalizes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+lattice"} modular law
            in lattices to more general relations, and which generalizes also so-called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+reciprocity"} Frobenius reciprocity
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+logic"} categorical logic
          %h2#definition Definition
          #Allegory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              An
              %strong allegory
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+posetal+2-category"} locally posetal 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              equipped with an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi o
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^o \colon A^{op} \to A
              which is the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity-on-objects"} identity-on-objects
            %ol
              %li
                the involution is order preserving and distributes over composition, i.e.
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ψ
                        %mi ϕ
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi o
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi ϕ
                          %mi o
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi o
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\psi\phi)^o = \phi^o\psi^o
              %li
                each
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-poset
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(x,y)
                has binary
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meet"} meets
              %li
                the
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+lattice"} modular law
                holds: for
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi x
                        %mo →
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi\colon x\to y
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi y
                        %mo →
                        %mi z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi\colon y\to z
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi χ
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi x
                        %mo →
                        %mi z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi\colon x\to z
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ψ
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ∩
                        %mi χ
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo ∩
                        %msup
                          %mi ψ
                          %mi o
                        %mi χ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi \phi \cap \chi \le \psi (\phi \cap \psi^o \chi)
          %p From these properties we immediately get that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi ψ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi o
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi o
                  %mo ∩
                  %msup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi o
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\phi \cap \psi)^o = \phi^o \cap \psi^o
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi χ
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mi χ
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi ψ
                  %mi χ
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mtext and
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mi χ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi χ
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ∩
                  %mi χ
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\phi \cap \psi) \chi \leq \phi\chi \cap \psi\chi
                  \\quad\text{and}\quad
                  \\chi (\phi \cap \psi) \leq \chi\phi \cap \chi\psi.
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p The first claim follows from the observation that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi χ
                            %mo ≤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo ∩
                            %mi ψ
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi o
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇔
                            %msup
                              %mi χ
                              %mi o
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo ∩
                            %mi ψ
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo .
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi o
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mtext monotone and involutive
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇔
                            %msup
                              %mi χ
                              %mi o
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mtext and
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msup
                              %mi χ
                              %mi o
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi ψ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mtext meet properties
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇔
                            %mi χ
                            %mo ≤
                            %msup
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mi o
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mtext and
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi χ
                            %mo ≤
                            %msup
                              %mi ψ
                              %mi o
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo .
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi o
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mtext monotone and involutive
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇔
                            %mi χ
                            %mo ≤
                            %msup
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mi o
                            %mo ∩
                            %msup
                              %mi ψ
                              %mi o
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mtext meet properties.
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\chi \leq (\phi \cap \psi)^o
                    \&amp;\iff
                    \\chi^o \leq \phi \cap \psi
                    \&amp;\quad&amp;(.)^o\;\text{monotone and involutive}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\iff
                    \\chi^o \leq \phi \; \text{ and } \; \chi^o \leq \psi
                    \&amp;&amp;\text{meet properties}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\iff
                    \\chi \leq \phi^o \; \text{ and } \; \chi \leq \psi^o
                    \&amp;&amp;(.)^o\;\text{ monotone and involutive}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\iff
                    \\chi \leq \phi^o \cap \psi^o
                    \&amp;&amp;\text{meet properties.}
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              For the claim
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi χ
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi χ
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi χ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi \cap \psi) \chi \leq \phi\chi \cap \psi\chi
              we use the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizontal+composition"} horizontal composition
              in a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+posetal+2-category"} locally posetal 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \cap \psi \leq \phi
              we get
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi χ
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi χ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi \cap \psi)\chi \leq \phi\chi
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi χ
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi χ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi \cap \psi)\chi \leq \psi\chi
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi χ
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi χ
                      %mo ∩
                      %mi ψ
                      %mi χ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\phi \cap \psi) \chi \leq \phi\chi \cap \psi\chi
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi χ
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi χ
                    %mi ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi (\phi \cap \psi) \leq \chi\phi \cap \chi\psi
              follows the the same arguments or by applying involution and the first claim.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Rel
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rel(C)
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+posetal+2-category"} locally posetal
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+relation"} internal relations
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Rel
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rel(C)
                is an allegory.
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+hyperdoctrine+with+equality"} first-order hyperdoctrine with equality
                similarly gives rise to an allegory, as does any abstract
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory+of+relations"} bicategory of relations
                in the sense of Carboni-Walters.
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+lattice"} modular lattice
                can be regarded as a one-object allegory if we take composition to be union and the involution to be the identity.
          %h2#maps_tabulations_and_units Maps, tabulations, and units
          %p
            A
            %strong map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\colon x \to y
            in an allegory is a morphism that has a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \dashv s
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi o
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s = r^o
            (hint: use the modular law to show
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∩
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi o
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \dashv s \cap r^o
            and
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∩
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mi o
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \cap s^o \dashv s
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit of the adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi x
                  %mo ≤
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi o
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} id_x \leq r^o r
            entails that the morphism is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entire+relation"} entire
            (sometimes also called
            = succeed ")" do
              %em total
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} counit of the adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi o
                  %mo ≤
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r r^o \leq id_y
            states the fact hat the morphism is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functional+relation"} functional
            (sometimes also called
            = succeed ")." do
              %em univalent
          %p
            Any 2-category has a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory+of+maps"} bicategory of maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \leq g
            then
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = g
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
          %p
            A
            %strong tabulation
            of a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
            is a pair of maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo =
                  %mi g
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mi o
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi = g f^o
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mi o
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∩
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mi o
                    %mi g
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^o f \cap g^o g = 1
            %strong tabular
            if every morphism has a tabulation, and
            %strong pretabular
            if every morphism is contained in one that has a tabulation.
          %p
            Every
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+regular+category"} locally regular category
          %p A locally regular category has finite products if and only if its tabular allegory of relations has top elements in its hom-posets.
          %p
            Finally, a
            %strong unit
            in an allegory is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_U
            is the greatest morphism
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\to U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            admits a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi\colon X\to U
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi X
                    %mo ≤
                    %msup
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mi o
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_X\le \phi^o\phi
          %p
            Thus, regular categories are equivalent to unital (or unitary) tabular allegories. For more details, see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories%2C+Allegories"} Categories, Allegories
            (
            %a{:href => "#FreydScedrov"}> Freyd-Scedrov
            ), the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
            (
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone"}> Johnstone
            ), or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/toddtrimble/published/Theory+of+units+and+tabulations+in+allegories"} Theory of units and tabulations in allegories
          %h2#division_allegories Division allegories
          %p
            A
            %strong union allegory
            is an allegory whose hom-posets have finite joins that are preserved by composition. Thus a union allegory is locally a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+lattice"} distributive lattice
            = succeed "." do
              %strong distributive allegory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+category"} coherent category
            (a “pre-logos”), and conversely the bicategory of relations in a coherent category is a (unitary tabular) distributive allegory. In particular, every unitary tabular union allegory is distributive, but in the non-tabular case this can fail: for instance, any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+lattice"} modular lattice
            can be regarded as a one-object union allegory and need not be distributive.
          %p
            A
            %strong division allegory
            is a distributive allegory in which composition on one (and therefore the other) side has a right adjoint (left or right division). That is: given
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r: A \to B
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \colon A \to C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi r
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s/r: B \to C
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi r
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \leq s/r \in \hom(B, C) \Leftrightarrow t \circ r \leq s \in \hom(A, C)
          %p
            (so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} - \circ r
            has right adjoint
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -/r
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extension"} Kan extension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \circ -
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo \
                  %mi u
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi u
                    %mi o
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi r
                    %mi o
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi o
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\backslash u \coloneqq (u^o/r^o)^o.
          %p In the bicategory of sets and relations, with notation as above, we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msub
                    %mo ∀
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s/r)(b, c) \dashv \vdash \forall_{a \colon A} r(a, b) \Rightarrow s(a, c)
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r(a, b)
            is shorthand for “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a, b)
            belongs to
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
          %p
            The category of maps (functional relations) of a unitary/unital tabular division allegory is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+category"} Heyting category
            (a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logos"}> logos
            ”), and conversely the bicategory of relations in a Heyting category is a unitary tabular division allegory. (
            %a{:href => "#FreydScedrov"}> Freyd-Scedrov
            , 2.32, p. 227.)
          %h2#power_allegories Power allegories
          %p
            A
            %strong power allegory
            is,
            = succeed "," do
              %em more or less
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            such that the inclusion functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mi Map
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: Map(\mathcal{A}) \to \mathcal{A}
            has a right adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            assigns to an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a power object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(A)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}
            for which the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi Rel
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: \mathbf{E} \to Rel(\mathbf{E})
            has a right adjoint
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Map
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Map(\mathcal{A})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \dashv P
            is fundamental.
          %p
            Since the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            is the identity on objects, the counit of the adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \dashv P
            at an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            may be written
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∋
                    %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ni_B: P(B) \to B
          %p
            and we have a kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comprehension+scheme"} comprehension scheme
            that to each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r: A \to B
            there is a unique map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi r
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_r: A \to P(B)
            %em characteristic map
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∋
                      %mi B
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r = \ni_B \circ \chi_r
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            are related by a property
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            there is a subobject
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_r(a)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            consisting of elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            so related to
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r = 1_A: A \to A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_{1_A}: A \to P(A)
            is called the
            %em singleton map
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_r
            may be defined as
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(r) \sigma_A
          %h3#freydscedrov_definition Freyd-Scedrov definition
          %p
            The exact definition of power allegory is a matter for consideration. One can get a certain distance just by adopting the naive definition suggested above, that a power allegory is nothing more than an allegory for which the inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Map
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Map(\mathcal{A}) \to \mathcal{A}
            has a right adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed "-allegory.)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
          %p
            Freyd and Scedrov start with a structure of division allegory (thus packing in a good amount of internal logic from the start) and introduce the fundamental adjunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \dashv P
            in terms of that structure. For them, a
            %em power allegory
            is defined to be a division allegory which associates to each object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∋
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ni_B \colon P(B) \to B
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \colon A \to B
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi A
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mo ∋
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∋
                      %mi B
                    %mo \
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_A \leq (r \backslash \ni_B) \circ (\ni_B \backslash r)
          %p
            which expresses the truth of the formula
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo :
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi B
                    %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mo ∋
                      %mi B
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_{a \colon A} \exists_{S: P(B)} \forall_{b \colon B} S \ni_B b \Leftrightarrow r(a, b)
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∋
                      %mi B
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mo ∋
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ∋
                      %mi B
                    %mo \
                    %msub
                      %mo ∋
                      %mi B
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi o
                    %mo ≤
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mrow
                        %mi P
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\ni_B \backslash \ni_B) \wedge (\ni_B \backslash \ni_B)^o \leq 1_{P(B)}
          %p
            which internalizes an axiom of extensionality, which reads
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mo ∋
                      %mi B
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mo ∋
                      %mi B
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊢
                    %mi S
                    %mo =
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \forall_{b \colon B} (S \ni_B b) \Leftrightarrow (T \ni_B b) \vdash S = T
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r: A \to B
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi r
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∋
                    %mi B
                  %mo \
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo \
                  %msub
                    %mo ∋
                    %mi B
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi o
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_r \coloneqq (\ni_B \backslash r) \wedge (r\backslash \ni_B)^o,
          %p
            which internalizes the formula-definition
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi χ
                      %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mo ∀
                      %mi b
                    %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mo ∋
                      %mi B
                    %mi b
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_r(a, S) \coloneqq \forall_b S \ni_B b \Leftrightarrow r(a, b)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_r
            is a map. (
            %a{:href => "#FreydScedrov"}> Freyd-Scedrov
            , pp. 235-236.)
          %p
            The bicategory of relations in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            is a power allegory; conversely, the category of maps in a unitary tabular power allegory is a topos.
          %h3#variant_notion Variant notion
          %p Nevertheless, the spare elegance of the naive definition gives one something to shoot for. It appears that quite a decent theory can be developed just by adding the assumption of coproducts in an allegory: a reasonable and fairly mild assumption. (Most allegories don’t admit many colimits; for example having coequalizers is pretty rare. But the standard examples do have finite coproducts, coinciding with coproducts on the maps/functional side.)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              A
              = succeed "-allegory" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              with finite coproducts
              %sup#fnref:1
                %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
              for which the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi Map
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: Map(\mathcal{A}) \to \mathcal{A}
              has a right adjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
          %p
            As before, the counit is denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∋
                    %mo :
                    %mi i
                    %mi P
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ni: i P \to 1_{\mathcal{A}}
            = succeed "-allegory" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Any
              = succeed "-allegory" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ni
              are satisfied.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_sketch Proof (sketch)
            %p
              For now we content ourselves with a description of the division structure. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r: A \to C
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s: B \to C
              be morphisms; we construct a right Kan lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo \
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \backslash r
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              through
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t: A \to B
              we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi t
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \circ t \leq r
              if and only if
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi s
                      %mo \
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t \leq s \backslash r
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %mo :
                      %mi P
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r = s = \ni_C: P C \to C
            %p
              Define the internal union
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcup_C
              by
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                        %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi P
                      %mi P
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi P
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcup_C = P(\ni_C): P P C \to P C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi C
                    %mo :
                    %mi P
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Rightarrow]_C: P C \to P C
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mi C
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∈
                            %mrow
                              %mi P
                              %mi C
                      %mi P
                      %mi P
                      %mi C
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                            %mi C
                      %mi P
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P C \stackrel{\in_{P C}}{\to} P P C \stackrel{\bigcup_C}{\to} P C
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∈
                      %mo ≔
                      %msup
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi o
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \in \coloneqq \ni^o
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo ⇐
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi C
                      %mo ≔
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo ⇒
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi C
                        %mi o
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Leftarrow]_C \coloneqq [\Rightarrow]_C^o
            %p
              We now show
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo ⇐
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %mo \
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Leftarrow]_C = \ni_C \backslash \ni_C
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo :
                      %mi P
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi P
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R: P C \to P C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∋
                      %mi C
                    %mi R
                    %mo ≤
                    %msub
                      %mo ∋
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ni_C R \leq \ni_C
              is equivalent to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo ⇐
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \leq [\Leftarrow]
              %em reflexive
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              where we have an actual equation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %mi R
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ni_C R = \ni_C
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(\ni_C) P(R) = P(\ni_C)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                        %mi C
                        %mi o
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(R) \leq \bigcup_C^o \bigcup_C
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mrow
                          %mi P
                          %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                        %mi C
                        %mi o
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                        %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mrow
                          %mi P
                          %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                        %mi C
                        %mi o
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo ⇐
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = \ni_C P(R) \sigma_{P C} = \ni_C \bigcup_C^o \bigcup_C \sigma_{P C} = \ni_C \bigcup_C^o = [\Leftarrow]
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              reduces to the reflexive case: form the reflexive completion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \vee R
              as the composite
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mi P
                            %mi C
                        %mo ,
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mi C
                    %mo +
                    %mi C
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ∇
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \stackrel{\langle 1_{P C}, R \rangle}{\to} C + C \stackrel{\nabla}{\to} C
            %p
              which is where coproducts come in; here
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
              is the codiagonal and we use the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo +
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C + C
              in an allegory is a biproduct to form the pairing for the first arrow. It is easy to show that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %mo ∨
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %mi R
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ni_C(1 \vee R) = \ni_C \vee \ni_C R = \ni_C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi R
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo ⇐
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \leq 1 \vee R \leq [\Leftarrow]
              from before. Thus we have shown
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo ⇐
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi C
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %mo \
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Leftarrow]_C = \ni_C \backslash \ni_C
            %p
              For general
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                      %mo ,
                      %mi s
                      %mo :
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r: A \to C, s: B \to C
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo \
                    %mi r
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \backslash r: A \to B
              is given by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi χ
                        %mi s
                        %mi o
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %mo \
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mi χ
                        %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_s^o (\ni_C \backslash \ni_C) \chi_r
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∋
                        %mi C
                      %msub
                        %mi χ
                        %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r = \ni_C \chi_r
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi s
                            %mi t
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                            %mi r
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇔
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ∋
                              %mi C
                            %msub
                              %mi χ
                              %mi s
                            %mi t
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                            %msub
                              %mo ∋
                              %mi C
                            %msub
                              %mi χ
                              %mi r
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇔
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ∋
                              %mi C
                            %msub
                              %mi χ
                              %mi s
                            %mi t
                            %msubsup
                              %mi χ
                              %mi r
                              %mi o
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                            %msub
                              %mo ∋
                              %mi C
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇔
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi χ
                              %mi s
                            %mi t
                            %msubsup
                              %mi χ
                              %mi r
                              %mi o
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                            %msub
                              %mo ∋
                              %mi C
                            %mo \
                            %msub
                              %mo ∋
                              %mi C
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⇔
                          %mtd
                            %mi t
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                            %msubsup
                              %mi χ
                              %mi s
                              %mi o
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mo ∋
                              %mi C
                            %mo \
                            %msub
                              %mo ∋
                              %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mi χ
                              %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    s t &amp;\leq r &amp;
                    \\;&amp;\iff &amp; \ni_C \chi_s t &amp;\leq \ni_C \chi_r
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp; \iff &amp; \ni_C \chi_s t \chi_r^o &amp;\leq \ni_C
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp; \iff &amp; \chi_s t \chi_r^o &amp;\leq \ni_C \backslash \ni_C
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp;&amp; \iff &amp; t &amp;\leq \chi_s^o (\ni_C \backslash \ni_C) \chi_r
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p thus proving the claim.
            %p
              Further details may be found
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/toddtrimble/published/Note+on+power+allegories"} here
          %p
            Thus the notion of
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
          %h2#syntactic_allegories Syntactic allegories
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+theory"} regular theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}_T
            given as follows:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the objects are finite strings of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sorts"} sorts
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %li
              %p
                a morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec X \to \vec Y
                is a predicate
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo ,
                      %mover
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(\vec x, \vec y)
                of sort
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo ,
                      %mover
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec X, \vec Y
                (or rather a provable-equivalence class of such predicates);
            %li
              %p
                the identity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vec X \to \vec X
                is (named by)
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ∧
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ∧
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1 = x_1 \wedge x_2 = x_2 \wedge \cdots \wedge x_n = x_n
            %li
              %p
                the composite of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \colon \vec X \to \vec Y
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \colon Y \to \vec X
                is named by
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∃
                        %mover
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo .
                        %mi R
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mover
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo ,
                        %mover
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mover
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo ,
                        %mover
                          %mi z
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists \vec y. R(\vec x, \vec y) \wedge S(\vec y, \vec z)
          %p
            That
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}_T
            is an allegory is B.311 in
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#FreydScedrov"} Freyd–Scedrov
          %p
            Further structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            gives rise to further structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}_T
            (B.313): if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+theory"} coherent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+theory"} first-order
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher-order+logic"} higher-order
            theory, then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}_T
            will be a distributive, division or power allegory respectively.
          %p
            Every pre-tabular allegory has a tabular completion, given by splitting its coreflexive morphisms (i.e. those endomorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            such that
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \subset id
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}_T
            is precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntactic+category"} syntactic category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %h3#the_existential_quantifier The existential quantifier
          %p
            There are two possible ways to interpret a regular formula of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∃
                  %mi y
                  %mo .
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exists y. R(x,y) \wedge S(y,z)
            in a unitary pre-tabular allegory, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            are interpreted as
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \colon X \to Y
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Y
                  %mo →
                  %mi Z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \colon Y \to Z
            respectively: as the composite
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \cdot r
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                pulling
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mi o
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^o
                back to the same hom set and taking their intersection:
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                          %mi o
                        %mi r
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∩
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi p
                          %mn 2
                          %mi o
                        %msup
                          %mi s
                          %mi o
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Z
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p_1^o r p_1) \cap (p_2^o s^o p_2) \colon X \times Z \to Y \times Y
            %li
              %p
                then forcing the two
                = succeed "s" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi Y
                          %mi o
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Y
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Y
                        %mo →
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_Y^o \colon Y \times Y \to Y
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo !
                        %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} !_Y
                to the unit, and post-composing with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mo !
                        %mi Z
                        %mi o
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} !_Z^o
                to get a morphism into
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            %li
              %p
                then forcing the
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
                in the domain to be equal to the
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
                in the codomain by taking the meet with
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi p
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi X
                        %mo ×
                        %mi Z
                        %mo →
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_2 \colon X \times Z \to Z
            %li
              %p
                and finally pulling back along (precomposing with the right adjoint of)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Z
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p_1 \colon X \times Z \to X
                to get a morphism
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Z
          %p We would like to know that these morphisms are equal, so that an existential formula will have a unique interpretation:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mi r
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∩
                    %msubsup
                      %mo !
                      %mi Z
                      %mi o
                    %msub
                      %mo !
                      %mi Y
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi Y
                      %mi o
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                      %mi o
                    %mi r
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                      %mi o
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mi o
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msubsup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                      %mi o
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s r = (p_2 \cap !_Z^o !_Y \Delta_Y^o ((p_1^o r p_1) \cap (p_2^o s^o p_2))) p_1^o
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p We show inclusion in each direction.
            %p
              Firstly,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mi r
                      %mo =
                      %mi s
                      %mi r
                      %mo ∩
                      %msub
                        %mi p
                        %mn 2
                      %msubsup
                        %mi p
                        %mn 1
                        %mi o
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s r = s r \cap p_2 p_1^o
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊤
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                        %mi Z
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∩
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mi o
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msubsup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                      %mi o
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\top_{Y Z} (r p_1 \cap s^o p_2) \cap p_2) p_1^o
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊤
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                        %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \top_{Y Z}
              is the top morphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi Z
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to Z
            %p Now we can calculate:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi s
                            %mi r
                            %mo ∩
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 2
                            %msubsup
                              %mi p
                              %mn 1
                              %mi o
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mi r
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∩
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msubsup
                              %mi p
                              %mn 1
                              %mi o
                          %mtd
                            %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                          %mtd
                            %mtext modular law
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mi r
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∩
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ∩
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msubsup
                              %mi p
                              %mn 1
                              %mi o
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi s
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi r
                            %msub
                              %mi p
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ∩
