          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dagger+2-poset"} dagger 2-poset
          %p Other attempted axiomatizations of the same idea “something that acts like the category of relations in a regular category” include:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory+of+relations"} bicategory of relations
                (a special sort of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+bicategory"} cartesian bicategory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category+equipped+with+relations"} 1-category equipped with relations
          %p Discussion of the relation between pretabular unitary allegories and bicategories of relations, and also between tabular unitary allegories and regular categories is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/toddtrimble/published/Theory+of+units+and+tabulations+in+allegories"} Theory of units and tabulations in allegories
          %h2#references References
          %p The standard monograph is
          %ul
            %li#FreydScedrov
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Freyd"} Peter Freyd
              and Andre Scedrov,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories%2C+Allegories"} Categories, Allegories
          %p The notion is discussed also in chapter A3 of
          %ul
            %li#Johnstone
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Johnstone"}> Peter Johnstone
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sketches+of+an+Elephant"} Sketches of an Elephant
          %p In
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bob+Walters"}> Bob Walters
              ,
              %em Categorical algebras of relations
              (
              %a{:href => "http://rfcwalters.blogspot.com/2009/10/categorical-algebras-of-relations.html"} blog post
              )
          %p
            it is shown that any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory+of+relations"} bicategory of relations
            is an allegory.
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allegory_%28category_theory%29"} Allegory
          %p An introduction headed towards applications in computer science and, in particular, fuzzy controllers can be found in
          %ul
            %li
              Michael Winter,
              %em Goguen Categories
              (2007)
